    "body": "Hey @KarlHeitmann, thanks for considering working on this!\r\n\r\nRather than a Daml file, you would probably need a Daml project (the source of information would be the `daml.yaml`, some sort of project manifest akin to a `package.json` for Node.js or a `pom.xml` for Maven projects). Daml projects use the language alongside an off-ledger counterpart, usually Java and/or TypeScript/JavaScript. You can have a fully working project locally by cloning https://github.com/digital-asset/ex-healthcare-claims-processing, which has all three languages co-existing in a single repository. There are other example projects you can clone in the https://github.com/digital-asset organization (the repository name for examples should always start with `ex-`).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
